{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"detached: true|process\\\\.kill\\\\(-|SIGKILL|wrangler.*dev|waitForMcpReady\\\" test packages --glob '*.ts' | head -80 && rg -n \\\"cloudflareWorkers\\\" . --glob '\"'!node_modules'\"' --glob '\"'!pnpm-lock.yaml'\"' | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"test/e2e/fixtures/stdio-server.ts:8: * (stdin EOF → SIGTERM → SIGKILL) is observable.\ntest/e2e/fixtures/stdio-server.ts:43:    // Misbehaving-server mode: keep alive after stdin EOF via interval (load-bearing — without it the child exits on stdin EOF and SIGTERM never arrives) and ignore SIGTERM, so only SIGKILL can end the process.\npackages/client/src/client/stdio.ts:250:                    processToClose.kill('SIGKILL');\ntest/integration/test/server/cloudflareWorkers.test.ts:33:async function waitForMcpReady(proc: ChildProcess): Promise<void> {\ntest/integration/test/server/cloudflareWorkers.test.ts:49:            throw new Error(`wrangler dev exited with code ${processExitedWithCode} before becoming ready.\\nstderr tail:\\n${stderrTail}`);\ntest/integration/test/server/cloudflareWorkers.test.ts:148:        // Start wrangler dev server. Readiness is determined by probing the MCP endpoint, not by\ntest/integration/test/server/cloudflareWorkers.test.ts:149:        // parsing wrangler's stdout — see waitForMcpReady for the reasoning.\ntest/integration/test/server/cloudflareWorkers.test.ts:150:        const proc = spawn('npx', ['wrangler', 'dev', '--local', '--port', String(PORT)], {\ntest/integration/test/server/cloudflareWorkers.test.ts:157:            await waitForMcpReady(proc);\ntest/e2e/scenarios/stdio.test.ts:99:        // Exit came from the EOF path, not the SIGTERM/SIGKILL escalation ladder.\ntest/e2e/scenarios/stdio.test.ts:172:    // SIGKILL escalation would only ever reach the npx wrapper while the real\ntest/e2e/scenarios/stdio.test.ts:207:        // termination below can only have come from the SIGKILL escalation.\ntest/e2e/scenarios/stdio.test.ts:215:            process.kill(childPid, 'SIGKILL');\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Sorunun kökü iki parçalı: `shell: true` ile öldürülen nesne yalnızca kabuk süreci olabiliyor, `workerd` torun olarak yaşamaya devam ediyor; ayrıca readiness hatasında cleanup yalnızca sinyal gönderip sürecin gerçekten kapanmasını beklemiyor. Ayrı bir process group oluşturup tüm gruba TERM→KILL kapanış protokolü uygulayacak ve cleanup’ı readiness beklenmeden önce kaydedecek şekilde düzeltiyorum."}}
